        {
          "q": "Use logarithm properties to expand $\\log\\left(\\dfrac{x^3\\sqrt{y}}{z^2}\\right)$ fully.",
          "answer": "$\\log\\left(\\dfrac{x^3\\sqrt{y}}{z^2}\\right)=\\log(x^3)+\\log(y^{1/2})-\\log(z^2)=3\\log x+\\dfrac{1}{2}\\log y-2\\log z$."
