          "q": "Solve $\\log(x)+\\log(x-3)=1$ for $x$, checking both solutions against the domain.",
          "answer": "Combine: $\\log[x(x-3)]=1$, so $x(x-3)=10$: $x^2-3x-10=0$, $(x-5)(x+2)=0$: $x=5$ or $x=-2$. Since $x>0$ and $x-3>0$ are required (domain of the original logs), $x=-2$ is rejected. Solution: $x=5$."
